  "sourceAssessment": {
    "capabilitySafety": "All new types and operations internal; deterministic fingerprint is domain-separated and length-prefixed correlation data. No actual issuer, publication I/O, source seal, registered consumer or engine activation is added.",
    "coordinates": "All seven source fields participate in action fingerprint; exact nonblank/non-control strings and positive turn/nonnegative incarnation required. Child request/token differ from parent and retain n/actionId with ordinal1. Recomputed record equality in event calculation checks full expected request value.",
    "lifecycle": "Duplicate refs and foreign turns fail before suppression. Consumed pure owner_turn_end is removed; independent mixed fields cause rejection requiring decomposition; separate time/source/scene/trigger/realm/condition/target events pass unchanged. Pending events remain subject to strict scheduler replay semantics.",
    "time": "None requires byte-identical sources/absence and carries supplied post-prefix result without reapplying timeChange. Incremental retains actual int delta, nullable epoch/effect value and existing resolver result. Absolute uses unchanged resolver policy, never infers elapsed minutes from jumps/rewinds. Calendar-only yields unresolved fallback and null effect time; reader-priority differences remain intentional.",
    "immutabilityAndNullBom": "Record fields are immutable scalar values; output list has independent read-only backing; input/output time arrays are cloned. Nullable absent world sources are retained. Existing CanonicalJsonUtf8 enforces one optional leading BOM and strict UTF8. Invalid command/state/coordinate/drift branches reject; some branches lack direct focused tests as O1.",
    "resolverPreservation": "The only existing production edit is private to internal on ResolveFrozenWorldTime. Its body/formulas and all existing consumers are byte-identical.",
    "gmSynchronization": "Spec/ledger explicitly identify intentional client-only foundation; no live GM schema, prompt, parser or player surface changed. Deferring prompt/examples is justified only for this bounded slice; live integration still requires same-change synchronization."
  },
  "fixtureAssessment": "New tests construct independent records, arrays, JsonObjects and sets; no shared mutable fixtures, owners or ordering. CreateCanonicalEffect allocates fresh structures. Tests call actual EffectLifecycleScheduler for turn advancement, replay rejection, deadline equality, scene expiry and unresolved time no_change; numeric expectations are literal, not read back from the subject. Source-loss pass-through is value-asserted, not a complete source-authority scenario. Existing progression neighbor uses fresh GUID directory/service per xUnit instance.",
